IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp6-interpretation`
IMPORT `cp6-social-insurance-number`
IMPORT `cp6-offences`
IMPORT `cp6-information`
IMPORT `cp6-accounts`
IMPORT `cp6-provinces-and-consent`
IMPORT `cp6-seat`

-- Worked cases for cp6-seat.l4: at least one case for every question, in the facts a real person in the seat would state.
-- Expected values are worked out by hand from the text (the working is beside each case) and never copied from the output.
-- The people: Ana (an employee in Ontario, born 15 March 2000), Ben (a self-employed carpenter), Chloe (an employee in Quebec).
-- The same facts are asked of the same person throughout where a question needs them.

§ `Cases -- the individual's questions on Part III`

§§ `Who administers the Act`

-- Ana asks who deals with her contributions (Part I) and who deals with her pension (everything else).
#ASSERT `Which Minister has control and direction of the part of the Act I am dealing with` TRUE EQUALS `the Minister of National Revenue`
#ASSERT `Which Minister has control and direction of the part of the Act I am dealing with` FALSE EQUALS `the Minister of Employment and Social Development`
-- Information about her earnings from her returns, obtained under the Act and needed for the Record, must be reported (s 92(2)(a)).
#ASSERT `Must the Minister of National Revenue report the information about me to the Minister` `earnings and contributions information needed for the Record of Earnings` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- General statistics need only be necessary for the administration (s 92(2)(c)).
#ASSERT `Must the Minister of National Revenue report the information about me to the Minister` `statistical and other general information necessary for the administration of the Act` FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Information of another kind is not within the subsection.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Minister of National Revenue report the information about me to the Minister` `information of another kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `May the report be made available to the Minister despite any other Act or law` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the report be made available to the Minister despite any other Act or law` TRUE FALSE)

§§ `My Record of Earnings`

-- Ana has had contributions deducted as an employee, applied in the way regulation 39 requires, and no agreement governs: she may require the statement.
#ASSERT `May I require the Minister to give me a statement of my earnings` TRUE FALSE 52000 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Ana's cousin has never contributed or had earnings attributed: not a contributor, no claim.
#ASSERT `May I require the Minister to give me a statement of my earnings` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Ben contributed on his self-employed earnings but applied by telephone, which is not the manner regulation 39 prescribes: no claim.
#ASSERT `May I require the Minister to give me a statement of my earnings` FALSE TRUE 31000 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Chloe's province has an agreement governing how she gets the statement: the Act alone does not say.
#ASSERT `May I require the Minister to give me a statement of my earnings` TRUE FALSE 40000 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Ana got the statement and is not satisfied: she may ask the Minister to reconsider it.
#ASSERT `May I ask the Minister to reconsider the statement of my earnings` TRUE FALSE 52000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I ask the Minister to reconsider the statement of my earnings` TRUE FALSE 52000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do sections 81 and 82 apply to my request as though it were an application for a benefit` TRUE
-- An entry made in 2020 can be questioned until 31 December 2024 and not after.
#ASSERT `What is the last day on which I may question an entry in my Record of Earnings` 2020 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2024 12 31
#ASSERT `Can I still question an entry in my Record of Earnings on that day` 2020 (YearMonthDay 2024 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I still question an entry in my Record of Earnings on that day` 2020 (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1))
-- The Minister has an employer's records showing 1,500 where the Record shows 1,000: the Minister may rectify upwards.
#ASSERT `May the Minister correct my Record of Earnings upwards` TRUE FALSE 1000 1500
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Minister correct my Record of Earnings upwards` FALSE FALSE 1000 1500)
-- Ben's entry came from his province's plan: it may be removed from the day the information was furnished.
#ASSERT `May the Minister remove the entry from my Record of Earnings on that day` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Minister remove the entry from my Record of Earnings on that day` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 9))
-- Another contributor's earnings were increased with earnings that were shown to Ana's account by mistake.
#ASSERT `Could the Minister reduce the earnings shown to my account` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Could the Minister reduce the earnings shown to my account` TRUE FALSE)
-- Ana's account shows 12,000, 2,500 of it by mistake: 9,500 after the correction.
#ASSERT `What would be shown to my account after the correction` TRUE 12000 2500 EQUALS 9500
#ASSERT `What would be shown to my account after the correction` FALSE 12000 2500 EQUALS 12000
-- Ana was told her earnings under section 96 and they have been reduced: the Minister must notify her, in writing at her latest known address.
#ASSERT `Must the Minister notify me of the reduction` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Minister notify me of the reduction` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Was the notice of the reduction given in the prescribed manner` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Was the notice of the reduction given in the prescribed manner` FALSE)
#ASSERT `May I ask the Minister to reconsider the reduction` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I ask the Minister to reconsider the reduction` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§§ `My Social Insurance Number`

-- Ana applied on 10 March 2026 to divide pensionable earnings and has no number: she must apply, by 9 April 2026.
#ASSERT `Must I apply for a Social Insurance Number because I applied for a division` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I apply for a Social Insurance Number because I applied for a division` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I apply for a Social Insurance Number because I applied for a division` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `By what date must I file my application for a Social Insurance Number because I applied for a division` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 9
-- Ana, born 15 March 2000, works in Ontario under a contract of service in pensionable employment and has no number: she must apply.
#ASSERT `Must I apply for a Social Insurance Number because I have reached eighteen and work in pensionable employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Chloe works in Quebec: section 4(1)(a) takes the duty out of Part III.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I apply for a Social Insurance Number because I have reached eighteen and work in pensionable employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A federal public servant in Quebec is back in, by section 4(2).
#ASSERT `Must I apply for a Social Insurance Number because I have reached eighteen and work in pensionable employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Ana started on 20 August 2019, long after reaching eighteen (treated as 1 April 2018): thirty days after 20 August 2019 is 19 September 2019.
#ASSERT `By what date must I file my application for a Social Insurance Number because I have reached eighteen and work in pensionable employment` (YearMonthDay 2000 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 9 19
-- Ben must file a return of self-employed earnings, has not applied for a division, works for no one, and has no number.
#ASSERT `Must I apply for a Social Insurance Number as a self-employed individual` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Ana, who is within subsection (2), is not within (3).
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I apply for a Social Insurance Number as a self-employed individual` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `By what date must I apply for a Social Insurance Number as a self-employed individual` (YearMonthDay 2027 6 15) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 6 15
-- Ana used the Minister's form and the prescribed manner; Ben used a form of his own.
#ASSERT `Is my application for a Social Insurance Number in the prescribed form and manner` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my application for a Social Insurance Number in the prescribed form and manner` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Must the Minister cause a Social Insurance Number to be assigned to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Minister cause a Social Insurance Number to be assigned to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `May a Social Insurance Number Card be issued to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May a Social Insurance Number Card be issued to me` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Ana's employer: must require her number, by 19 September 2019 (the later of reaching eighteen and starting), and keep a record.
#ASSERT `Must my employer require me to tell them my Social Insurance Number` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my employer require me to tell them my Social Insurance Number` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `By what date must my employer require me to tell them my Social Insurance Number` (YearMonthDay 2000 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 9 19
#ASSERT `Must my employer keep a record of my Social Insurance Number` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my employer keep a record of my Social Insurance Number` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Her employer required her on 5 February 2026: she must tell them by 7 March 2026.
#ASSERT `Must I tell my employer my Social Insurance Number` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I tell my employer my Social Insurance Number` FALSE)
#ASSERT `By what date must I tell my employer my Social Insurance Number` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 5) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 7
-- Her application was signed in her own hand; Ben's grandfather cannot sign and made his mark before two witnesses who signed.
#ASSERT `Is my application for a Social Insurance Number signed as the Act requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my application for a Social Insurance Number signed as the Act requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE 2 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my application for a Social Insurance Number signed as the Act requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE 1 TRUE)
-- Ana changes her name on 1 June 2026 while employed in Ontario: she must tell the Minister by 31 July 2026.
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Minister my new name and by what date` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS `the individual must inform the Minister by a last day` WITH `last day for informing the Minister` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 31
-- Chloe changes her name the same day while employed in Quebec: Part III does not reach her employment, and no later event has come.
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Minister my new name and by what date` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS `no time for informing the Minister has yet begun to run`
-- Ben already told the other authority: nothing to tell.
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Minister my new name and by what date` TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS `the individual need not inform the Minister of the new name`
-- Ben was not employed that day but later started pensionable employment on 15 September 2026: sixty days later is 14 November 2026.
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Minister my new name and by what date` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 9 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS `the individual must inform the Minister by a last day` WITH `last day for informing the Minister` IS YearMonthDay 2026 11 14
#ASSERT `Is a number assigned through my province's authority treated as assigned under this Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a number assigned through my province's authority treated as assigned under this Act` FALSE)

§§ `Offences and prosecution`

#ASSERT `Am I guilty of an offence for false or misleading information in my application for a Social Insurance Number` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence for false or misleading information in my application for a Social Insurance Number` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of an offence for applying again for a Social Insurance Number` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence for applying again for a Social Insurance Number` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- The Act states a maximum of $100 only for the employer's offence.
#ASSERT `What is the greatest fine the Act states for the offence` `an employer's failure to comply with subsection 98(5) or a regulation under paragraph 101(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `What is the greatest fine the Act states for the offence` `furnishing false or misleading information in an application for a Social Insurance Number` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The thing arose on 10 March 2021: a prosecution can be commenced until 10 March 2026.
#ASSERT `What is the last day on which I could be prosecuted for the offence` (YearMonthDay 2021 3 10) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `Can I still be prosecuted for the offence on that day` (YearMonthDay 2021 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I still be prosecuted for the offence on that day` (YearMonthDay 2021 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11))
-- Ben is a director of a corporation that commits an offence and authorized it.
#ASSERT `Am I a party to and guilty of my corporation's offence` TRUE TRUE `authorized the commission of the offence`
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a party to and guilty of my corporation's offence` TRUE TRUE `took none of those parts`)
#ASSERT `Does section 41(6) apply to the information or complaint against me` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 41(6) apply to the information or complaint against me` FALSE)

§§ `Who may see my information; agreements; oaths`

-- Ana's earnings information, obtained by an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency for the administration of the Act, goes to an officer of Employment and Social Development.
#ASSERT `May information about me be passed from one federal department to another` `the Canada Revenue Agency` TRUE TRUE `the Department of Employment and Social Development` TRUE TRUE
-- The Department of Employment and Social Development is not a department that may pass it back.
#ASSERT NOT (`May information about me be passed from one federal department to another` `the Department of Employment and Social Development` TRUE TRUE `the Canada Revenue Agency` TRUE TRUE)
-- An outside person who is not an officer or employee cannot receive it.
#ASSERT NOT (`May information about me be passed from one federal department to another` `the Canada Revenue Agency` TRUE TRUE `another body` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `May information about me obtained under section 104.1 be made available to another person or body` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May information about me obtained under section 104.1 be made available to another person or body` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May information about me obtained under section 104.1 be made available to another person or body` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May information about me be given to my province's pension plan authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May information about me be given to my province's pension plan authority` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `May I be given my statement of earnings by my province's pension plan authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I be given my statement of earnings by my province's pension plan authority` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `May the Minister or my province's authority act on my request to reconsider a statement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Minister or my province's authority act on my request to reconsider a statement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- An official authorized by the Minister of National Revenue, acting in the course of their employment, may take Ana's oath for Part I; another Act limits the other official.
#ASSERT `May the official take my oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation` `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part I or its regulations and authorized by the Minister of National Revenue` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the official take my oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation` `neither of those` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the official take my oath, affidavit, declaration or solemn affirmation` `employed in the administration or enforcement of Part III and Part II or their regulations and authorized by the Minister` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Chloe lives in Canada and an agreement with another country is in force.
#ASSERT `May an agreement with another country provide for my benefits to be extended, increased or decreased` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May an agreement with another country provide for my benefits to be extended, increased or decreased` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

§§ `Gifts to the Minister`

#ASSERT `Must the Minister dispose of what I give subject to my terms` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Minister dispose of what I give subject to my terms` FALSE TRUE)

§§ `My contribution, and the rates`

-- Ana's base contribution goes to the Canada Pension Plan Account; her first additional contribution to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account.
#ASSERT `Into which account of Canada is my contribution credited` `the base tier` EQUALS `the Canada Pension Plan Account`
#ASSERT `Into which account of Canada is my contribution credited` `the first additional tier` EQUALS `the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account`
#ASSERT `Into which account of Canada is my contribution credited` `the second additional tier` EQUALS `the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account`
-- Ana's base rate in 2026 is 4.95%; Ben's first additional rate for 2022 was 1.5%; there is no second additional rate for 2023.
#ASSERT `What contribution rate do the Schedules set for me for the year` `the base tier` `contributing as an employee` 2026 EQUALS JUST (4.95%)
#ASSERT `What contribution rate do the Schedules set for me for the year` `the first additional tier` `contributing as a self-employed person` 2022 EQUALS JUST (1.5%)
#ASSERT `What contribution rate do the Schedules set for me for the year` `the second additional tier` `contributing as an employee` 2023 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What contribution rate do the Schedules set for me for the year` `the second additional tier` `contributing as a self-employed person` 2024 EQUALS JUST (8.0%)
-- A change to 5.05%, 5.05%, 10.1% from 4.95%, 4.95%, 9.9% is within the limits; to 5.1%, 5.1%, 10.2% is not.
#ASSERT `Is the change of the contribution rates for the year within the limits` (5.05%) (5.05%) (10.1%) (4.95%) (4.95%) (9.9%)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the change of the contribution rates for the year within the limits` (5.1%) (5.1%) (10.2%) (4.95%) (4.95%) (9.9%))
-- For the period 2025 to 2027 a regulation made on 30 September 2027 comes into force on 1 January 2028; one made on 1 October 2027 is not covered.
#ASSERT `When does a regulation changing the contribution rates come into force` 2025 (YearMonthDay 2027 9 30) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2028 1 1)
#ASSERT `When does a regulation changing the contribution rates come into force` 2025 (YearMonthDay 2027 10 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Rates found insufficient: 8.8% less 0.6% is 8.2%, below 8.4%; no recommendation takes the case out.
#ASSERT `Are the contribution rates found insufficient, so that Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended` (8.8%) (0.6%) (8.4%) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- ... unless an increase was recommended and made in time.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the contribution rates found insufficient, so that Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended` (8.8%) (0.6%) (8.4%) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- The third case (10.4% gives A = 5.2%, B = 4.9%): year 1 is 4.99%, year 2 is 5.035%; the self-employed rate in year 3 is twice 5.075%.
#ASSERT `What contribution rate applies to me for the year after the rates are deemed amended` `contributing as an employee` (10.4%) (0%) (4.9%) 1 EQUALS JUST (4.99%)
#ASSERT `What contribution rate applies to me for the year after the rates are deemed amended` `contributing as an employer` (10.4%) (0%) (4.9%) 2 EQUALS JUST (5.035%)
#ASSERT `What contribution rate applies to me for the year after the rates are deemed amended` `contributing as a self-employed person` (10.4%) (0%) (4.9%) 3 EQUALS JUST (10.15%)
#ASSERT `What contribution rate applies to me for the year after the rates are deemed amended` `contributing as an employee` (10.4%) (0%) (4.9%) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Chloe's province took over the plan after notice on 15 June 2026: from 1 January 2029 the Act no longer owes the benefit from her Quebec contributions.
#ASSERT `Has the Act stopped owing the benefit attributable to my contributions in my province` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2029 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the Act stopped owing the benefit attributable to my contributions in my province` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2028 12 31))
-- A notice laid in 2026: the earliest day is 1 January 2029.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest day the change may come into force` 2026 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2029 1 1
#ASSERT `May the provision come into force on that day` TRUE FALSE 2026 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2029 1 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the provision come into force on that day` TRUE FALSE 2026 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2028 12 31) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the provision come into force on that day` FALSE FALSE 2026 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the Act of Parliament need the consent of the provinces` `the general level of benefits provided by the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the Act of Parliament need the consent of the provinces` `some other matter` EQUALS JUST FALSE
